index 4736d79..274b477 100644
--- a/docs/production-telemetry.md
+++ b/docs/production-telemetry.md
@@ -69,3 +69,17 @@ remains available for development and CI, but synthetic scores are not productio
   the action path has been tested against a disposable target and reviewed.
 - Model buffers and latest predictions must be persisted or explicitly treated as ephemeral;
   in-memory state is not durable across API restarts.
+
+## Building training data from your own host
+
+The API stores every polled sample in `telemetry_samples`. To turn that into a training file:
+
+1. Record each real incident with `scripts/annotate_incident.py add ...` (start, end, category, evidence).
+2. Run `docker compose --profile training run --rm build-training-data --scope host`. A minute is
+   `is_unhealthy` only inside a confirmed incident window; the file is written with
+   `data_source=production`. The script refuses to write when there are too few confirmed incidents.
+3. Run the trainer (`docker compose --profile training run --build --rm trainer`). The model is
+   promoted only if it passes the quality gates; then `/ready` clears for that scope.
+
+The dashboard's synthetic simulation is a separate, opt-in demo: `docker compose --profile demo run
+--build --rm demo-model`. It never affects production readiness.
